{{Quote|Tyranus wanted Sifo-Dyas dead. The Pykes were well paid to shoot down his ship.|[[Lom Pyke]]|<ref name="The Lost One" />}}
Concurrent to the [[Invasion of Naboo|blockade of Naboo]], [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Finis Valorum]] sent [[Jedi Master]] [[Sifo-Dyas]] on a secret '''mission to Oba Diah'''.<ref name="Timelines" /> Sifo-Dyas, who was sent without the knowledge of the [[Jedi High Council|Jedi Council]], traveled with Valorum's aide [[Silman]] to resolve a dispute within the [[Pyke Syndicate]], one that threatened to spark a crime war beneath the streets of [[Coruscant]]. However, before Sifo-Dyas could negotiate, the [[Jedi]] Council requested that he [[Mission to Felucia (Sifo-Dyas)|travel]] to [[Felucia]] to resolve a tribal dispute. As he and Silman were leaving, intending to return, the [[Pyke]]s&mdash;at the behest of a figure known as [[Dooku|Tyranus]], secretly the former Jedi Dooku and an agent of the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]]&mdash;shot Sifo-Dyas' ship down. Sidious, who wanted to eliminate Dyas so that the Sith could take control of the creation of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]],<ref name="The Lost One" /> had Dooku betray and kill him. 

By that point, the Naboo Crisis had [[Battle of Naboo|concluded]], with Dooku's decision to shoot down Sifo-Dyas an act of fealty towards Sidious.<ref name="Timelines" /> The Jedi Master was killed in the crash,<ref name="Creation of the Clone Army">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-inside-intel-the-creation-of-the-clone-army|text=''Star Wars'' Inside Intel: The Creation of the Clone Army|int=Star Wars Inside Intel}}</ref> but Silman survived, becoming a prisoner of the Syndicate until being [[Mission to Oba Diah (Clone Wars)|discovered]] by the Jedi during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="The Lost One" /> Taking possession of Dyas' corpse<ref name="Creation of the Clone Army" /> from the Pykes, Dooku subsequently posed as a Jedi and deceitfully staged Sifo-Dyas' death on Felucia to conceal what had transpired. [[Sifo-Dyas's lightsaber]] was left behind at the crash site, however.<ref name="The Lost One" />

